# UNDER 8'S DAY

Celebrate Under 8's with Drumming Singing and Dancing!

![](/media/2020/02/day_care_img_17-scaled.jpg)

Experience West African Drum & Dance first hand. Watch incredibly skilled artists deliver your school with an interactive high energy performance.

Learn to play a rhythm on West African djembe and then dance the corresponding dance to that rhythm. Loads of drums, percussion, singing and movement!

Choose your date and discuss your school schedule and requirements. Speak with a Rhythm Culture artist directly. No booking companies.

## About Us

[Rhythm Culture’s](/) Drum Sing Dance program is packed full of interactive fun, educational and multicultural. With so many different countries, instruments and dances to choose from, we  guarantee your school an action packed under 8's day celebration. Engage students and their parents with loads of fun and high energy entertainment whilst learning about the amazingly diverse cultures that live in West Africa.

[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zcPZmbtX0L8&t=6s](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zcPZmbtX0L8&t=6s)

![](/media/2020/02/day_care_bg_02.png)

## What Happens?

-   Every child will play an African drum & unique African percussion.
-   45 – 60 minute workshop
-   There will be body percussion
-   Lots of singing, dancing & laughing
-   African dance moves
-   Call and response music patterns
-   We ask lots of questions
-   The children will go on a journey through story, song & movement
-   Learn about how and what the African instruments are made from

[Contact Us](/contact-us/)

## Drum Sing Dance Program Benefits:

**Musical**  – drumming, singing, and lots of instruments

**Physical** – dancing, coordination, spacial awareness

**Interactive** – every child has an instrument to play

**Educational** – counting, language, listening, directions

**Social** – teamwork, communication, connection, community

**Cultural** – learn about African culture through stories and play

**Creative** – thinking, playing and movement

